course: dictionary
lesson: 14589
title: Pliers: a tool with two jaws
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pliers are a hand tool with two handles and two jaws. You squeeze the handles, and the jaws close on whatever is between them. «Mum used pliers to grip the bent nail and pull it out of the wood.» Grip means hold tightly, so the pliers hold the nail firmly.
explain: Pliers can do four jobs with wire: grip it, bend it, twist it and cut it. «Ben cut the wire with pliers, then bent the end into a neat hook.» The words cut and bent are your clues: they tell you what the tool does to the wire.
explain: Pliers is always plural, even for one tool. You say «a pair of pliers», not «a plier». «I need a pair of pliers to fix the bike chain.»
explain: In science, pliers are a lever. A lever turns a small push into a bigger push somewhere else. Squeezing the handles makes a much bigger force at the jaws, which is why pliers can grip something hard.
fact: Pliers are a hand tool with two handles and two jaws.
fact: «Pliers» means a tool used for gripping, bending, twisting or cutting wire.
fact: Pliers is a plural noun, so say «a pair of pliers».
fact: In science, pliers are a lever: a small force on the handles makes a bigger force at the jaws.
fact: Check a word by swapping in your meaning: «I used a pair of pliers to bend the wire» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
exercise: What are pliers? | A kind of bird that lives near water | A small wooden ladder | A type of cold drink | *A hand tool with two handles and two jaws
exercise: «I need ___ to fix the bike chain.» Which phrase is correct? | two pliers each | a plier | a pliers | *a pair of pliers
exercise: Why can pliers grip something hard? | The handles are very light | *Squeezing the handles makes a bigger force at the jaws | The jaws are made of soft paper | Pliers stay open all the time
test: «Mum used pliers to grip the bent nail.» What does grip mean here? | *Hold tightly | Throw far away | Count slowly | Paint brightly
test: Which part of pliers grips the wire? | *The jaws | The paint on the handles | The handles | The metal pin in the middle
exam: «Ben cut the wire with pliers, then bent the end into a hook.» Which job did Ben NOT do with the pliers? | *Painted the wire | Bent the wire into a hook | Cut the wire
